diff --git a/docs/inventory-screen.md b/docs/inventory-screen.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..63fd6f9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/inventory-screen.md
@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@
+# Inventory screen
+
+The inventory screen shows all ten block types and how many of each the player has. It shows
+which blocks are still locked and the level that unlocks each one, and it lets the player pick
+the block to build with. Most players are kids on phones, so the screen is built for touch first,
+with big targets, short words and pictures before text. Mouse and keyboard, and controllers, get
+the same screen with their own shortcuts.
+
+Code: `src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/UI/`, started from `Main.client.luau` by
+`InventoryScreen.start()`.
+
+## What's on screen
+
+**Blocks button.** This button is always on screen at the right edge, halfway up. That keeps it
+clear of the phone thumbstick (bottom left) and the jump button (bottom right). It shows a 3D cube
+of the block you're building with and how many you have left, so it is also the "current block"
+display.
+
+**Panel.** The panel opens over a dimmed backdrop. It has:
+
+- A header with "My Blocks", the player's level (⭐ Level 3) and a red ✕ close button.
+- A grid of tiles, one per block type, in hotbar order. Each tile has a 3D preview, the name, and
+  then either a count (×48) or a padlock with the unlocking level (🔒 Level 6).
+  - The block in use has a green border and a ✓ badge.
+  - Locked tiles are darker and the preview is greyed out.
+  - Blocks you have none of show ×0 in red, but you can still pick them.
+- A footer that says how to pick a block on the device you're using. It briefly turns yellow to
+  explain why a locked block can't be picked, for example "🔒 Ice unlocks at Level 4".
+
+The grid has five columns on wide screens and drops to as few as two on narrow ones, so tiles never
+get smaller than a thumb. It scrolls when the tiles don't all fit, as on a landscape phone. All
+sizes scale with screen height, so text is readable on a phone and on a TV across the room. The
+button and panel stay inside the device's safe area and below the Roblox top bar.
+
+## Opening and closing
+
+| | Touch | Mouse and keyboard | Controller |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Open | Tap the Blocks button | Click the Blocks button, or press **E** | Press **Y** |
+| Close | Tap ✕, or tap the dimmed area outside the panel | Click ✕ or outside the panel, or press **E** again | Press **B** (or **Y** again) |
+| Close by picking | Tap an unlocked block | Click an unlocked block | Press **A** on an unlocked block |
+
+Picking a block always closes the screen, so building again takes one tap. Opening the Roblox
+menu (Esc, or the Roblox button) also closes the screen.
+
+While the screen is open:
+
+- Tapping or clicking the world doesn't place blocks. Placing comes back on close, unless something
+  else had turned it off.
+- The mouse is freed from first person and shift lock.
+- The character can still walk; the screen doesn't pause the game.
+
+## Actions on each input
+
+### Touch
+
+- **Pick a block:** tap its tile. The whole tile is the button, never less than about 88 points
+  wide, twice Apple's 44-point minimum touch target.
+- **Locked block:** tapping it doesn't pick it. The footer says which level unlocks it.
+- **See more blocks:** drag the grid up and down when it doesn't all fit.
+- The screen shows no key or button hints on touch.
+
+### Mouse and keyboard
+
+- **Pick a block:** click its tile. Hovering a tile gives it a white border and makes it a little
+  bigger.
+- **Shortcuts:** an **E** chip on the Blocks button and on ✕ shows the open and close key.
+- **Number keys:** keys **1–9** and **0** still pick hotbar slots directly, as before. Each
+  unlocked tile shows its number in the top-left corner.
+- **Hints:** the footer reads "Click a block to build with it · E to close".
+
+### Controller
+
+- **When the screen opens:** the tile of the block in use is focused (white border, a little
+  bigger). Pressing **A** straight away keeps the current block.
+- **Move around:** use the D-pad or left stick. Focus stays inside the panel and the grid scrolls
+  to follow it.
+- **Pick or close:** **A** picks the focused block. **B** closes without changing anything.
+- **Button hints:** the Blocks button and ✕ show the **Y** and **B** glyphs, and the footer shows
+  **A** Choose / **B** Close. Glyphs come from `UserInputService:GetImageForKeyCode`, so
+  PlayStation controllers get their own symbols.
+- **On close:** focus is cleared, so **A** goes back to jumping.
+
+The hints follow the device the player last used. Picking up a controller mid-game switches every
+hint to controller glyphs at once, and the screen focuses a tile if it is open.
+
+## Accessibility
+
+- Locked, selected and empty states never rely on color alone. Each also has a symbol or text
+  (🔒, ✓, ×0).
+- The open and close pop animations are skipped when Reduced Motion is on in Roblox settings.
+
+## Known gaps
+
+- `BlockPlacer`'s number keys can still select a locked block, because it doesn't know about
+  `BlockInventory`. The screen hides the number hint on locked tiles, but the keys themselves
+  aren't blocked.
+- `BlockPlacer` only places blocks with a mouse click or a tap. Controllers can pick a block here
+  but can't place it yet.
+- The server doesn't check locks or counts when placing.
